  "gaps": [
    "Elective credit amount (46) is not printed for this program; it is derived from 120 total minus 36 major credits (30 core + 3 capstone + 3 related) minus 38 remaining general education credits. The program table prints only 'Remaining General Education and Elective Courses 84'. The general catalog range is 1–49.",
    "The 3-credit general education Mathematics requirement is not listed separately. The capture says STAT 200 'may be applied to general education requirements', and the course sequence maps it to 'Related and general education/mathematics'. The ledger therefore counts STAT 200 toward Mathematics.",
    "The capture does not explicitly label the credit unit as semester hours.",
    "Residency rules are not tied to specific courses, so all requirements are marked institutionalOnly false: at least 30 credits (normally the final 30) must be completed at UMGC; half the credits within the major must be completed at UMGC; at least 15 upper-level credits (300–499) must be completed at UMGC.",
    "At least half the major credits must be earned through graded coursework. A minimum grade of C is required for courses applied to the major, and a 2.0 overall GPA is required.",
    "WRTG 112 must be completed with C- or better within the first 24 credits and may not be earned through Prior Learning. Mathematics must be completed within the first 24 credits. The professional exploration course must be taken within the first 6 credits.",
    "General education courses may not be taken pass/fail. Pass/fail credit (max 18) applies only to electives.",
    "The capture does not state which specific courses satisfy flexible slots beyond discipline lists. PSYC 251, PSYC 310 and PSYC 341 may each be replaced by any upper-level PSYC course."
  ],
